    {
      "id": "claim_c759a01604224bd396fd1cf8c3600cf1",
      "statement": "The release pipeline is two-phase: a push to candidate builds every native target, attests provenance, and uploads to a DRAFT GitHub release plus a container smoke build; publishing the draft is a separate human-approved action, and a failed candidate is deleted without main ever moving; the release body is derived from the release commit message (subject dropped, trailers stripped).",
